# "Islandwalk" names a basic land type, a word of Lord of Atlantis's text (CR 612.1-612.2): when Trait Doctoring replaces
# Island with Swamp in the Lord's text on turn 3, its "Other Merfolk ... have islandwalk" reads "... have swampwalk", and
# Cenote Scout has swampwalk instead (CR 702.14a). Bot2 controls a Swamp and no Island, so its Misshapen Fiend can't block
# the Scout (the refusal; CR 702.14c) - with islandwalk it could have - while it may block the Lord (the positive
# control). The Fiend (1/1) dies to the Lord, the Lord takes 1, and the Scout deals 2: Bot2 goes to 18.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Lord of Atlantis
Cenote Scout
Island
Island
Island
Trait Doctoring
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Misshapen Fiend
Swamp x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lord of Atlantis.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cenote Scout.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Misshapen Fiend.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Cenote Scout.Keywords = Islandwalk
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Trait Doctoring.Cast(Lord of Atlantis)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a basic land type)
Bot1.Modes(Island)
Bot1.Modes(Swamp)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Cenote Scout.Keywords = Swampwalk
Bot1.Attack(Cenote Scout; Lord of Atlantis)
! Bot2.Block(Misshapen Fiend > Cenote Scout)
Bot2.Block(Misshapen Fiend > Lord of Atlantis)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Graveyard = Misshapen Fiend
Bot1.Battlefield.Cenote Scout.Keywords = Swampwalk
Bot1.Battlefield.Cenote Scout.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Lord of Atlantis.Damage = 1
